Who needs to complete this task?

    Cluster administrator A cluster administrator must complete this task.
When do you need to complete this task?

    This task is optional but strongly recommended. If you do not validate the health of your cluster before you upgrade IBM Software Hub, you might encounter issues during the upgrade.

    Repeat as needed If you have multiple instances of IBM Software Hub, repeat this task for each instance of IBM Software Hub that you plan to upgrade.

Before you begin
Best practice: You can run the commands in this task exactly as written using the installation environment variables. Ensure that you added the new environment variables from Updating your environment variables script.

In addition, ensure that you source the environment variables before you run the commands in this task.
About this task
Before you upgrade IBM Software Hub, you can run the following commands to check the health of your cluster:

    Use the cpd-cli health cluster command to check that cluster resources, such as operators and machine config pools are healthy.
    Use the cpd-cli health nodes command to check that the nodes are ready and that resource use on each node is under 90%.
    Use the cpd-cli health network-performance command to check that your cluster network has sufficient throughput.
    Use the cpd-cli health network-connectivity command to check the state of cluster network resources.

Procedure

    Log the cpd-cli in to the Red Hat® OpenShift® Container Platform cluster:

    ${CPDM_OC_LOGIN}

    Remember: CPDM_OC_LOGIN is an alias for the cpd-cli manage login-to-ocp command.
    Run the cluster command:

    cpd-cli health cluster

    Confirm that the cluster resources report returns the expected results:
    Test
    	
    What the test checks
    	
    Expected result
    Cluster Version Check	The cluster is running a supported version of Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform.	[SUCCESS]
    Image Registry Connectivity Test	The cluster can reach the following sites:
        https://icr.io
        https://github.com/IBM
        https://mirror.openshift.com/pub
    Note: In a restricted network, this check might fail. If you pull images from a private container registry, [FAIL] is an acceptable result.
    	[SUCCESS]
    Machine Config Pools Healthcheck	The machine config pools are not UPDATING or DEGRADED. 	[SUCCESS]
    Certificate Signing Request Healthcheck	There are no certificate signing requests that are pending.

    If there are pending certificate signing requests, the check fails.
    	[SKIP...]
    Cluster Operator Healthcheck	The cluster operators are AVAILABLE and are not DEGRADED.	[SUCCESS]
    ETCD Healthcheck	The Kubernetes etcd cluster members are healthy.	[SUCCESS]
    Run the nodes command:

    cpd-cli health nodes

    Confirm that the node resources report returns the expected results:
    Test
    	
    What the test checks
    	
    Expected result
    Node readiness	The cluster nodes are READY and are not under pressure. 	[SUCCESS]
    Node Resources Healthcheck	That resource use on each node is under 90%. 	[SUCCESS]
    Run the network-performance command.
    The cluster pulls images from the IBM Entitled Registry

    The cluster pulls images from a private container registry

    Confirm that the summary section of the network performance report includes the expected results:
    Test
    	
    What the test checks
    	
    Expected result
    Node readiness check	The nodes that will be tested are READY. (By default, all nodes are tested.)	[SUCCESS]
    Pod readiness check	The pods that are used to test network performance are ready and that their containers are running.

    The ibm-network-performance-ds DaemonSet creates a pod on each node that will be tested. (By default, all nodes are tested.)
    	[SUCCESS]
    Network throughput check	The minimum network throughput is at least 350 MB per second. 	[SUCCESS]
    Run the network-connectivity command.

    cpd-cli health network-connectivity \
    --control_plane_ns=${PROJECT_CPD_INST_OPERANDS}

    Confirm that the summary section of the network connectivity report includes the expected results:
    Test
    	
    What the test checks
    	
    Expected result
    Network Cluster Operator Healthcheck	The OpenShift cluster network operators are AVAILABLE and are not DEGRADED.	[SUCCESS]
    Pod Healthcheck	The pods in the openshift-ovn-kubernetes project are healthy.	[SUCCESS]
    PodNetworkConnectivityCheck Custom Resource Healthcheck	The podnetworkconnectivitychecks objects are reachable.	[SUCCESS]
    Operator To Operand Pod Connection check	The pods in the operators project for the instance can connect to pods in the operands project for the instance.	[SUCCESS]

What to do next
Now that you've checked the health of your cluster, you're ready to complete Reauthorizing an instance administrator with the minimum RBAC to upgrade components (Upgrading from Version 5.1 to Version 5.3).
